# Independent T1 criteria (written before reading compiler diff)

Controlling texts read: spec types/subtyping/inference/rules, expressions/operators, patterns/coverage, services/errors/Assert and host boundary; literal-types design and joint-design contracts. Spec wins. T2/T3 future syntax is not a T1 acceptance requirement.

1. Int/String types denote exact All, finite, or cofinite sets. Canonical numbers (hex/decimal, negative zero, arbitrarily large) and decoded Unicode share identities. Set union, meet, difference, subtyping and runtime tests must agree. Arithmetic/concatenation produce whole Int/String; only negation of an integer literal (through groups) is singleton.
2. Inference must retain principal schemes, variance and value restriction. No context-dependent inferred literal widening or library-specific rules. Known facts are separate: hidden callback/continuation/service inputs must not cause false disjointness, singleton bounds, wrong field types, or omitted checks. Test folds with scalar, tuple, list, optional and record-of-functions accumulators, recursive functions, generic/invariant wrappers, and changes from adding/removing correct annotations.
3. E0520 only where top-level known value sets are actually disjoint. Check direct literals, variables, function results, generalized unknown parts, arithmetic, complements, callbacks and recursive groups. Nested literals alone do not establish disjointness of tuples/custom types.
4. One unguarded clause (including choices) is fitted, may require Assert, and is not exhaustive matching. Other blocks must cover every inferred input; guards cannot cover. Check Int/String finite/cofinite/whole inputs, catchalls, prefixes, nested constructors/tuples, shared generic fields, and lists with literal heads. Known documented limitation: list/shared fields need explicit finite input if only literal branches cover them. Report that as usability cost, not an implementation violation.
5. Narrowing must subtract only values fully taken by prior unguarded rows, considering all other columns. Test negative types, prefix/complement combinations, guard interference and list lengths; no reachable value may acquire Never. Deferred fitted-pattern failure paths must survive recursion/groups and own Assert frames.
6. Error rows may narrow literal errors; service arguments remain equal/invariant. Generic records of getters/setters and functions cannot lose relevant variables during display/generalization.
7. Host-provided restricted literals must be rejected (external results, host service results/errors, export inputs); outbound finite/cofinite values are allowed. Alias/union syntax must preserve this policy and actual runtime tag tests.
8. Package interfaces must retain all literal members beyond hover limits, canonicalize spelling/sets, preserve imported exactness and detect changes beyond truncation. Human display must sort and escape properly without altering schemes.
9. Compare examples/std/bench acceptance with redesign. Explain actual everyday regressions and diagnostics. Audit at least 40 changed golden lines across files against their recorded rules.
10. Measure distinct literal unions and literal matches at increasing sizes (250/500/1000 and larger where practical), include times. Accepted suspect programs run at O0 and O2, checking semantics and unexpected traps. Diagnostics should identify the failing source and meaningful missing value.

Only demonstrated new problems will be findings; distinguish execution, code evidence, and inference. Do not edit tracked files or commit. All probes/logs under /tmp/review-t1/; cargo only through authorized heavy+direnv wrapper.
